# `real` is the exact reals' type (decision real-canonical): type(π) is real, every number is a real, Real its
# foreign spelling, a float given to a real parameter the exact real
'type(π)'	'real'
'π is real'	yes
'3 is real'	yes
'(1/3) is real'	yes
'"a" is real'	no
'x: real = sqrt(2); x * x == 2'	yes
'x: Real = sqrt(2); x as text'	'√2'
'g(b: real) := b; g(2.5)'	2.5
